      ],
      "source": "https://mercedcountytimes.com/the-town-of-el-nido-thats-spanish-for-the-nest/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened in 1920, marking its growth after irrigation enabled intensive farming in the early 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Nido%2C_Merced_County%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A large cotton gin was built in 1937, reflecting cotton’s role as the principal crop before dairy expanded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Nido%2C_Merced_County%2C_California",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During World War II, the U.S. Army operated Potter Auxiliary Field nearby, training pilots from 1942 to 1945.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Nido%2C_Merced_County%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "El Nido’s historic Catholic church still hosts services in an altar that dates back to the town’s founding era.",
